The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```
if (!(map->m_flags & EROFS_MAP_META)) {
    while (1) { /* lookup existing pcluster */ }
}
...
if (!fe->pcl->from_meta) {
    /* bind cache */
} else {
    ret = erofs_init_metabuf(&map->buf, sb, erofs_inode_in_metabox(fe->inode));
    if (ret) return ret;
    ptr = erofs_bread(&map->buf, map->m_pa, false);
    if (IS_ERR(ptr)) {
        ret = PTR_ERR(ptr);
        erofs_err(sb, "failed to get inline folio %d", ret);
        return ret;
    }
    WRITE_ONCE(fe->pcl->compressed_bvecs[0].page, map->buf.page);
}
```
Reason:
The original code reads inline data **after** the pcluster has been allocated and added to I/O chains (e.g., via `fe->head = fe->pcl` in the EEXIST path). If a fatal signal interrupts `erofs_bread()`, the function returns an error, but the pcluster is already linked into a chain. Later, `z_erofs_decompress_queue()` accesses `compressed_bvecs[0].page`, which remains NULL because the assignment was skipped, causing a NULL pointer dereference.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
if (map->m_flags & EROFS_MAP_META) {
    ret = erofs_init_metabuf(&map->buf, sb, erofs_inode_in_metabox(fe->inode));
    if (ret) return ret;
    ptr = erofs_bread(&map->buf, map->m_pa, false);
    if (IS_ERR(ptr)) {
        erofs_err(sb, "failed to read inline data %pe @ pa %llu ...", ptr, ...);
        return PTR_ERR(ptr);
    }
    ptr = map->buf.page;
}
...
if (!fe->pcl->from_meta) {
    z_erofs_bind_cache(fe);
} else {
    folio_get(page_folio((struct page *)ptr));
    WRITE_ONCE(fe->pcl->compressed_bvecs[0].page, ptr);
    ...
}
```
Reason:
The inline data is now read **before** the pcluster is looked up or registered, and the page pointer is stored locally. If the read fails, the function returns early without adding any pcluster to an I/O chain, preventing a later dereference of an invalid page pointer. The stored pointer is later used to set `compressed_bvecs[0].page` only after the pcluster is successfully registered or reused. This ensures that by the time the pcluster becomes part of a chain, its compressed vector is already valid.

